┌─ publish ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── gdoc v2.9.0 ─┐
│ Build the note as a house-style document and upload it into one folder.                          │
│ ▸ gdoc v2.10.0 is published and this is v2.9.0. gdoc update installs it.                         │
├─ Usage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ gdoc publish --md <file> --folder-id <folder id> [--house <file>]                                │
├─ Flags ─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ --md <file>             │ the note to publish                                                    │
│ --folder-id <folder id> │ the Drive folder the document is created in                            │
│ --house <file>          │ a house style file other than the one inside gdoc                      │
├─ Every command takes ───┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ --config <file>         │ the settings file to use instead of settings.yaml in the config folder │
│ --mark <text>           │ the mark gdoc writes in front of its words in a thread; an empty mark  │
│                         │ writes the words alone, and then nothing in the thread says which      │
│                         │ words are gdoc's                                                       │
└─ Example ───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
gdoc publish --md note.md --folder-id 1AbC...
Add --json to print the JSON object a skill reads.
